<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-no</span></b> , āvi, 1, v.
		n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to swim out</i>, <i>swim away</i>, <i>escape by
			swimming.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Prop. (rare but class.):
			facile, * <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 1, 2, 81</span></i>: e concha,
			* <i><span class="en">Cic. Fin. 3, 19, 63</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Erythraeam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 28</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in terram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					33, 41</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b> transf., of flying, * <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3,
			591</span></i>; * <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 12,
			95</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to traverse by
			swimming</i>, i. e. <i>to sail through</i> a place
			(in post-Aug. poets): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orbem fretis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 5, 316</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">has valles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 662</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
